Let heights be a list of 1, 8, 6, 2, 5, 4, 8, 3, and 7.
Let n be count of heights.
Let best area start at 0.

For every i from 0 to n - 1:
    For every j from i + 1 to n - 1:
        Let low height be item i of heights.
        If item j of heights < low height:
            Set low height to item j of heights.
        Let area be (j - i) * low height.
        If area > best area:
            Set best area to area.

Print best area.
